sequenceDiagram
    participant Admin as Admin / kubectl
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Operator as Grid Operator<br/>9090/TCP Metrics
    participant SWIM as SWIM Runtime<br/>7946/UDP AES-256-GCM
    participant Peer as Peer Site Operator<br/>7946/UDP AES-256-GCM
    participant Scoring as Scoring Engine
    participant CM as ConfigMap<br/>(Routing Overlay)
    participant Sync as overlay-sync Sidecar
    participant GW as Praxis AI Gateway
    participant Enrollment as Enrollment Server<br/>HTTPS mTLS
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP TLS

    Note over Admin,GW: Flow 1: Overlay Rendering

    Admin->>K8sAPI: Create InferenceProvider CR
    K8sAPI-->>Operator: Watch event (InferenceProvider)
    Operator->>SWIM: Propagate provider state
    SWIM->>Peer: CRDT delta replication<br/>7946/UDP AES-256-GCM
    Peer-->>SWIM: Peer provider state<br/>7946/UDP AES-256-GCM
    SWIM-->>Operator: Merged distributed state
    Operator->>Scoring: Score providers<br/>(noMetrics / queueDepth / kvCachePressure)
    Scoring-->>Operator: Scored provider list
    Operator->>K8sAPI: Write ConfigMap (SSA)<br/>versioned routing overlay
    K8sAPI-->>Sync: Watch event (ConfigMap)
    Sync->>GW: Write overlay to filesystem
    Note right of GW: Hot-reload routing<br/>without restart

    Note over Admin,PG: Flow 2: Site Enrollment

    Admin->>Enrollment: POST /v1alpha1/enrollmenttokens<br/>mTLS client cert
    Enrollment->>PG: Persist token<br/>5432/TCP TLS
    PG-->>Enrollment: Token stored
    Enrollment-->>Admin: One-time enrollment token

    Note over Operator,PG: New site joins

    Operator->>Enrollment: POST /v1alpha1/enrollments<br/>HTTPS CA-pinned + one-time token
    Enrollment->>PG: Record enrollment<br/>5432/TCP TLS
    Enrollment->>K8sAPI: Create site identity Secret
    Enrollment-->>Operator: mTLS identity certificate issued
    Operator->>SWIM: Join gossip mesh<br/>with site identity
    SWIM->>Peer: Announce new site<br/>7946/UDP AES-256-GCM

    Note over Admin,GW: Flow 3: Cross-Site Routing (data plane context)

    participant Client as External Client
    participant ConsumerGW as Consumer Gateway
    participant ProviderGW as Provider Gateway<br/>(remote site)
    participant Backend as Inference Backend

    Client->>ConsumerGW: Inference request<br/>HTTPS TLS
    ConsumerGW->>ProviderGW: Forward request<br/>443/TCP mTLS (grid identity)
    ProviderGW->>Backend: Backend call<br/>HTTP/HTTPS Bearer/API key/SigV4
    Backend-->>ProviderGW: Inference response
    ProviderGW-->>ConsumerGW: Response (mTLS)
    ConsumerGW-->>Client: Inference result
